# condor_submit_dag sweep_fraction.dag : the decade at full resolution (4096 px, 60 rings) with facular fractions
# (faculae='fraction': every bright pixel is min(|B|/mu/B_sat, 1) facula, no area threshold), the sets of
# parameters_fraction.txt (noise_th, I_th, B_sat, Temp)
#   1. the grids once per T_sp (build_grids_fraction.sub; shared with sweep_4096.dag)          } at the same time
#   2. identification in 80 blocks of days, all the sets of thresholds at once (identify_fraction.sub) }
#   3. the days still missing and the filling factors of every set, one job per set (aggregate_fraction.sub)
#   4. one simulation per line of parameters_fraction.txt: light curve, RV, FWHM, BIS, contrast, CCF, MAD / RMS
#      (run_opt_rv_fraction.sub)
#   5. table of all the sets and the figures (collect_stats_fraction.sub; it runs even if some sets failed)
JOB grids     build_grids_fraction.sub
JOB ident     identify_fraction.sub
JOB aggregate aggregate_fraction.sub
JOB sets      run_opt_rv_fraction.sub
JOB collect   collect_stats_fraction.sub
PARENT ident CHILD aggregate
PARENT grids aggregate CHILD sets
PARENT sets  CHILD collect
SCRIPT POST ident /bin/true
SCRIPT POST sets  /bin/true
